@using BlazorRamp.DocSite.Pages.GettingStarted
@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_CSS_Classes}/{GlobalValues.CSS_Path_Part_Section}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Api}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Section @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.CSS_Name_Section @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Api_Usage</h1>

<p>
    Everything you need to work with the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-section</span> CSS class: the BEM classes it provides, the strongly-typed <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Section</span> C# object
    used to apply them, supporting enums, and the CSS variables used for styling.
</p>

<h2 class="page-heading">Overview</h2>

<p>
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-section</span> is a general-purpose content block used for page sections, cards, and other bordered or coloured content areas.
    It's the same block used throughout the Blazor Ramp documentation site itself.
</p>
<p>
    Colours and backgrounds are theme-reactive: they're built from the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-cls-*</span> variables described below, which in turn derive from the same
    <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">--br-unit-*</span> primitives  used across every Blazor Ramp component. Changing your theme updates <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">br-section</span> automatically
    - no separate configuration needed.
</p>


<section>
    <h2 id="c#-classes" class="page-heading">C# API</h2>
    <p>
        <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Section</span> provides the BEM CSS classes for the br-section block: a general-purpose,
        theme-reactive content section used for page content, cards, and other bordered or coloured content areas.
    </p>
